NV_PK(14,{"this stone wall by the front gate has two gold words that mean the dragon sings below them a dragon flies among clouds and waves this wall stands next to the dragon door":"","on the other side the gold words mean the tiger roars and two tigers walk under pine trees this wall is next to the tiger door people say you should walk in through the dragon door and walk out through the tiger door":"","this round stone by the door looks like a drum so it is called a drum stone it is carved from stone and helps keep the door post steady":"","look at the edge of the roof each round tile end shows the character for long life above them are painted flowers and a carved openwork panel":"","look up at the front gate the blue plaque says mazu's goodness matches heaven the gold carvings beside the door are full of bats in chinese the word for bat sounds like the word for good luck so bats bring good luck":"","stories and flowers are painted all along the beams and two carved dragon heads hang down from them":"","turn around and look back at the gate this blue plaque from 1868 says mazu's goodness is as great as that of nuwa legend says nuwa mended the sky":"","from the courtyard look up at the roof a flaming pearl sits in the middle of the ridge the four gold words wish everyone in this land by the sea a happy spring together":"","look up a little crouching figure seems to hold up the roof corner on his shoulders people call him the foreigner carrying the temple corner stories differ some link him to the time of dutch rule and others say he is a strong temple guardian":"","under the eaves a gold lion lies on the beam and gold openwork carvings fill the space below in the left corner you can see the little figure holding up the roof":"","in this old painting the god of long life holds a peach a crane and two children are with him peaches and cranes both stand for a long life it is signed yufeng the painter chen yufeng made paintings for this temple's main hall":"","the roof corner carrier":"","under the roof corner a little crouching figure seems to carry the beam people call him the foreigner carrying the temple corner stories about him differ":""});